# The table editor, a mission made of sentences (tests/demo/pinball3d_editor_rules.sh). Written by guided.py.
# "+mission" adds one, with a step; its name is typed. The step becomes "Hit ...": its event is chosen in the list
# of events, and the editor gives it the first group that can be hit, the bumpers.
4 key g meta
5 text +mission
6 key Enter
8 key f meta
9 text name
11 key Tab
12 text "Deep Scan"
13 key Enter
15 key f meta
16 text steps[0].event
18 move 1300 112
19 down
20 up
22 text hit
23 key Enter
# Two more steps, each added by its event in the list the button Add opens. A ball that rolls over a switch: the editor
# gives the lanes. A hit again, of the standup targets this time, found in the list of what can be hit; twice; and the
# light that blinks while it is the step to do, chosen among the lights. No text is typed: the panel will ask for
# "Hit pops", "Roll over lanes", "Hit stand 2 times".
25 key f meta
26 text steps
28 move 1394 118
29 down
30 up
32 text roll
33 key Enter
35 key f meta
36 text steps
38 move 1394 118
39 down
40 up
42 text hit
43 key Enter
45 key f meta
46 text steps[2].on
48 move 1300 112
49 down
50 up
52 text stand
53 key Enter
55 key f meta
56 text steps[2].count
58 key Tab
59 text 2
60 key Enter
62 key f meta
63 text steps[2].light
65 move 1300 112
66 down
67 up
69 text bankArrow
70 key Enter
# The mission goes first, so that a game starts with it: the whole form again (Escape in the box that finds a field),
# then the arrow under its title, once per mission before it.
73 key f meta
74 key Escape
76 move 1190 295
77 down
78 up
